  message: "ROOT CAUSE FOUND 2026-09-04 (bisected Source/Core/Session.swift by prefix, first erroring prefix ends at line 509): a conditional-compilation block inside the class body -- '#if canImport(Darwin) && !canImport(FoundationNetworking)' wrapping 'open func webSocketRequest' -- is not parsed by tree-sitter-swift; error recovery re-parents the class header ('open class Session: @unchecked Sendable {' becomes simple_identifier + ERROR spanning lines 30-511) and the class's members surface under ERROR nodes, so no class symbol is minted and its methods are kinded as top-level functions. A 3-line class with the same header parses clean; the '#if' inside the body is the trigger. Consequences beyond symbol extraction: the receiver-type scoping in swift.py treats a declaration under an ERROR as file-level and walks lookups through ERRORs (PR for the registry consumer), which keeps 'rootQueue.async' typed in this file, but sites whose declarations are re-parented arbitrarily still lose (part of the 105 residual losses on Alamofire). Fix shape: pre-strip '#if/#else/#endif' directive lines inside type bodies before parsing (keeping line numbers by replacing them with blank lines), or teach the grammar; the former is local and testable."  # ce45
